00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:05.150 align:start position:0%
Iran says two missiles hit an Iranian  tanker overnight off the coast of Saudi  Arabia in a new escalation of tensions  in the region  Iran's state-run news agency says the  ship was sailing near the Saudi port of  Jeddah the tanker company says the crew  is safe the US Navy says it's aware of  the incident the reported attack comes  just weeks after drone and missile  attacks on the world's largest oil  processing facility in Saudi Arabia in  July the u.s. accused Iran of attacking  oil tankers near the Strait of Hormuz  Tehran denies any responsibility
 

